{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And He will destroy.</b> He will cut off, like וכל חרם (Leviticus 27:29), that Israel will pass through it on dry land and the sea will not hinder them from returning speedily:" "<b>בעים.</b> It has no parallel; the mem is a root letter, and its meaning is like בכח (in strength). Those who explain it from the root of אם תבעיון בעיו (Isaiah 21:12) do not know grammar." "<b>The river.</b> It is the יאור (the Nile)." "<b>And He shall cause to tread.</b> A verb with two objects."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:28.226673331Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}